<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">veil-sight</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Veil Sight</ansi> spell opens the caster's perception to the hidden layer of
reality, allowing them to pierce illusions and detect concealed enemies.
While active, hidden creatures in the same room are revealed.

This is an essential buff when venturing into areas known to shelter
stealthy enemies -- particularly tunnels, bandit roads, and other zones
where ambushers lurk.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast veil-sight</ansi>     Grants yourself see-hidden for its duration.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">4</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Self only</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Defense:     </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">None -- help spells always apply</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Duration:    </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Scales with spellcasting skill</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Effect:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">See-hidden: reveals concealed creatures in your room</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">4</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Divination</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - Hidden mobs will attack on entry if you don't detect them first.
  - Even with Veil Sight active, detection on entry is an opposed roll
    (Perception + Search vs Dex + Skullduggery). Higher perception helps.
  - Refreshing the spell before it expires is cheaper than fighting from
    a surprised state.

